invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_addcarry.c
catches: rsa_addcarry_equiv_test
reason: the square's doubling drops the top bit of each odd word of the
  cross products, the bit that moves into the next even word, so the
  square is short by a power of two whenever that bit is set.
  bin/rsa_addcarry_equiv_test holds rsa_mont64_addcarry_square to the
  rows' multiplication of a by itself and to rsa_mont64.c's loops at every
  word count.

--- old
        addcarry_word low = (t[2 * i] << 1) | moved;
--- new
        addcarry_word low = (t[2 * i] << 1) | (moved & 0);
